  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Some hypotheses are naturally one-sided. For example, we may wish to test whether heritability $ h^2 $ is significantly different from zero. In this case, true values of $ h^2 < 0 $ cannot occur, so that the alternative to the null hypothesis $ h^2 = 0 $ is $ h^2 > 0 $.",
      "source_page": 882,
      "printed_page": 862,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p882:b15"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        137.0,
        1311.0,
        1095.0,
        1437.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Consider the null hypothesis that the test statistic has mean $ \\mu = \\mu_0 $ versus the alternative hypothesis that $ \\mu = \\mu_1 $, where (for example) $ \\mu_1 > \\mu_0 $. Suppose that",
      "source_page": 882,
      "printed_page": 862,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p882:b16"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        138.0,
        1441.0,
        1097.0,
        1506.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FIGURE:A5.2]]",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b3"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        109.0,
        351.0,
        974.0,
        412.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "under the null hypothesis, the test statistic $ T \\sim \\mathrm{N}(\\mu_o, \\sigma_o^2) $, so that $ (T - \\mu_o)/\\sigma_o $ is distributed as a unit normal, implying from Equation A5.1b that",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        62.0,
        473.0,
        1021.0,
        539.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_appendix1_formula259]]",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b5"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        171.0,
        562.0,
        824.0,
        633.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, comparing the observed statistic T with the $ \\alpha $-level critical value, $ T_{c}(\\alpha) $, where",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        61.0,
        654.0,
