        716.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_appendix1_formula260]]",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        403.0,
        720.0,
        677.0,
        754.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "gives the one-sided test of significance with probability $ \\alpha $ of a false positive. We reject the null hypothesis when $ T > T_c(\\alpha) $.",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b10"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        61.0,
        767.0,
        1020.0,
        831.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Suppose that the alternative hypothesis is correct, so that $ T \\sim \\mathrm{N}(\\mu_1, \\sigma^2) $. What is the probability that the resulting test statistic is significant (and hence a false negative is avoided)? Since it is now $ (T - \\mu_1)/\\sigma_1 $ that follows a unit normal, the probability that the test statistic exceeds the critical value $ T_c(\\alpha) $ given by Equation A5.2b is",
      "source_page": 883,
      "printed_page": 863,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p883:b11"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        61.0,
        831.0,
